# devtools/vacuum/VACUUM.pin -- the vacuum release the openapi-lint CI job
# (.github/workflows/ci.yml) and `make openapi-lint` run, and the SHA-256 of
# each release archive they may download. devtools/vacuum/install.sh reads
# it, downloads vacuum_<version>_<os>_<arch>.tar.gz from the GitHub release
# and refuses to install unless the archive's SHA-256 equals the value here.
# These values are the trust anchor: they were checked against the release's
# checksums.txt and the GitHub release asset digests when the pin was taken.
# Bump procedure: devtools/vacuum/README.md.
#
# Format: KEY=value, one per line, no quotes, no spaces; '#' starts a comment
# line. sha256_<os>_<arch> uses the release's own asset names (linux_x86_64,
# linux_arm64, darwin_x86_64, darwin_arm64). An OS/arch with no line here is
# refused, not downloaded unverified.
version=0.42.3
sha256_linux_x86_64=31d647c75daa4924f5d5b2fe48b3be8e54a910494d5f278039899a36653037f7
sha256_linux_arm64=597c2b74e4f19a7ee1aead1c968a2bf2a6b409581721bef9c298b5c660af6860
sha256_darwin_x86_64=775cb522b2d2c3d6b1ee380f10dfecba9660fbd8b5d01e625fb709b2d067a127
sha256_darwin_arm64=c851191eaa0e9464be97d9f0a2a7c4a4904f834a3a9c420f604e2f1e339275e6
